---
// For parents (bedtime.md §2.4): under 250 words; confirmed names only.
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, PROJECT_CREDIT, SITES, siteUrl } from "@goldstein/config/sites";
import { loadManifest } from "@goldstein/data/load";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// AI-improved sound paragraph only once the switch exists (docs/design/ai-audio.md §3.1).
const hasCleanAudio = (loadManifest().counts.clean_audio ?? 0) > 0;
---

<Base page="about" title="For parents">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">For parents</h1>
    <p>
      {SITES.bedtime.name} plays the Goldstein family's recorded stories at bedtime. Most are told
      by <strong>Uncle Yossi</strong> (Rabbi Yosef Goldstein) on his radio show{" "}
      <em>Tzivos Hashem on the Air</em>, 1981 to 1992, and by his son{" "}
      <strong>Rabbi Chaim Levi Goldstein</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>How the playlists are chosen</h2>
    <p>
      Every morning there are new playlists: Tonight's Mix first, then four chosen by age and mood,
      each ending with calmer stories, and Radio Night, whole episodes of the radio show. The first
      stories of a playlist don't come back for weeks. Little Ones is about an hour and a half; the
      others about two hours. A story with something a parent may want to know about has a small ⓘ
      in the list.
    </p>

    <h2>The recordings</h2>
    <p>
      These are 1980s radio broadcasts and family tapes, as they were. Nothing is cut or changed, so
      you may hear a song, a little hiss, or a radio station's sound.
    </p>
    {hasCleanAudio && (
      <p>
        If the hiss bothers you, turn on <strong>AI-improved sound</strong> in the player. A
        computer program has rebuilt the voices from each tape so they come through clearer. Voices
        can sound a little different, and songs may come out oddly. The original tapes are kept as
        they were; switch it off to hear them. The setting stays on this phone, for this site only.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2>At bedtime</h2>
    <p>
      Tap a playlist, set the sleep timer, and put the phone down. The screen goes dark by itself.
      To keep the site one tap away, use your browser's “Add to Home Screen”.
    </p>

    <h2>More stories</h2>
    <p>
      Children can browse on <a href={siteUrl("kids", "/")}>{SITES.kids.name}</a>. Every recording,
      with transcripts, is in <a href={siteUrl("library", "/")}>{SITES.library.name}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions, or a tape we're missing? <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      No cookies, no accounts, no tracking.
    </p>
    <p>{PROJECT_CREDIT}</p>
  </article>
</Base>
